Connect Phase 1 — register the `connect` scope in the shared shell.

FOUR files, and it has to be all four. The scope union appears in AppShell,
Sidebar and Topbar independently; missing one is a type error at that file
only, which reads as "Connect is broken" rather than "one union is stale".

The fourth change is the one that fails SILENTLY: Sidebar's `logo` ternary
picks the brand lockup by scope and falls back to Core. Add the scope to the
union but not the ternary and Connect compiles, runs, and quietly wears the
Core logo — which is exactly the bug docs/CONNECT_BRIEF.md §6 warns about.

lib/nav.tsx gains connectNav() only. RAIL_PRODUCTS.connect is deliberately
LEFT at live:false — flipping it is the launch switch and belongs in the
commit that has Amit's logo pair and Core's sign-off on the guest path, not
in this one.

Needs from Amit before that flip:
  - apps/web/public/brand/connect-logo.png  (mark, 32px)
  - apps/web/public/brand/connect-name.png  (wordmark, dark on transparent, 30px)
  - a tile colour that is not #00b8d9 — Family already owns that cyan, and
    tile colour is how people find an app in a grid without reading it.

Apply from the repo root:  git apply connect-phase1-0005-shell-scope.patch

